# The on-screen keyboard when the physical keyboard goes away while a field is open (the owner's case on the deck, 0.1.0),
# through the app's real policy: input.state written as the launcher writes it (a new file, a new gen), read by
# _common's osk_policy on the monotonic clock, the shared rule (cp0_app_osk_allowed). For the editor, Open or create and
# New note: a field asks for the keyboard while a keyboard is there (nothing shows, the request is held: osk_req); the
# keyboard goes away: the on-screen keyboard shows by itself within about 1.5 s; a keyboard comes back: it goes. A
# Bluetooth keyboard that went away 2 min ago counts as asleep for 10 min (the shared rule: every app the same): nothing
# shows, a tap on the field asks again (still nothing), Settings > On-screen keyboard says why; gone 700 s ago: it shows.
seed note "Field log.md" field.md
wait 900
# ---- the editor
key ctrl-p
type field log
key enter
wait 500
expect state page preview
key ctrl-e
wait 500
expect state page editor
expect osk_allowed no
expect osk off
expect state osk_req editor
expect state kbd 1
keyboard off gone 30
wait 400
expect osk_allowed yes
expect osk on
expect state kbd 0
expect has "Hold 3 s: options"
shot 01-editor-keyboard-gone
check editor-keyboard-gone
keyboard on
wait 400
expect osk off
expect state osk_req editor
expect state kbd 1
# a Bluetooth keyboard gone 2 min ago: asleep; a tap on the text asks again: still nothing
keyboard off btgone 120
wait 400
expect osk_allowed no
expect osk off
tapat 0.5 0.4
wait 600
expect osk off
expect state osk_req editor
# its 10 minutes are over (gone 700 s ago): the keyboard shows by itself
keyboard off btgone 700
wait 400
expect osk_allowed yes
expect osk on
# a 3 s hold on the text with the keyboard up: the options box (the keyboard goes for it, and comes back after it); the
# cursor does not move
mark
holdat 0.5 0.25 3300
wait 400
expect state popup menu
expect same cursor
key esc
wait 600
expect state popup none
expect osk on
# the keyboard's Esc puts it away (the request goes); a tap on the text asks again
tapkey "Esc"
wait 500
expect osk off
expect state osk_req -
tapat 0.5 0.3
wait 600
expect osk on
expect state osk_req editor
tap "Esc"
wait 600
expect state page home
expect osk off
# ---- Open or create
keyboard on
wait 300
key home
key enter
wait 500
expect state page open
expect osk off
expect state osk_req open
keyboard off gone 30
wait 400
expect osk on
shot 02-open-keyboard-gone
check open-keyboard-gone
keyboard on
wait 400
expect osk off
expect state osk_req open
# its Enter put the keyboard away; a tap on the field asks again
keyboard off gone 30
wait 400
expect osk on
tapkey "<enter>"
wait 500
expect osk off
tapfield 1
wait 600
expect osk on
expect state osk_req open
tap "Esc"
wait 500
expect state page home
# ---- New note
keyboard on
wait 300
key home
key down
key down
key down
key down
key enter
wait 500
expect state page new
expect osk off
expect state osk_req new
keyboard off gone 30
wait 400
expect osk on
shot 03-new-keyboard-gone
check new-keyboard-gone
keyboard on
wait 400
expect osk off
keyboard off btgone 120
wait 400
expect osk off
tapfield 1
wait 600
expect osk off
expect state osk_req new
keyboard off gone 30
wait 400
expect osk on
tap "Esc"
wait 500
expect state page home
# ---- Settings > On-screen keyboard says what the rule says, and why
keyboard on
wait 300
key end
key enter
wait 500
expect state page settings
key end
key end
wait 300
expect text "On-screen keyboard"
expect text "allowed: no"
expect text "^a keyboard is connected"
shot 04-settings-keyboard-there
keyboard off btgone 120
wait 1200
expect text "allowed: no"
expect text "^Bluetooth keyboard asleep 8 min more"
shot 05-settings-bluetooth-asleep
check settings-osk
keyboard off gone 30
wait 1200
expect text "allowed: yes"
expect text "input.state keyboards=0 vkb=auto"
shot 06-settings-allowed
